title: _path_to_aad answers '' for an empty path where Go answers ':'
updated: 2026-08-21T09:20:32Z
---

Measured at karr #36 (docs/adr/0044, measurement 3), against sops 3.13.3.

Go builds the AAD as strings.Join(path, ":") + ":", so a leaf at the DOCUMENT ROOT authenticates under ":". File::SOPS::_path_to_aad has an early return:

    return "" unless $path && @$path;

so it answers the empty string for the same leaf. Measured on real documents: an env comment (root) decrypts under ":" and NOT under ""; a YAML comment on the first line of a file is also ":"; inside map: it is "map:" and inside list: it is "list:", which _path_to_aad already reproduces.

WHY NOTHING IS BROKEN TODAY. A leaf at the root is unreachable in YAML and JSON -- a document is a mapping, so every leaf has at least one key. The one place it occurs is an env comment, and Format::ENV puts those under the EMPTY KEY, so the path is [""] and _path_to_aad returns ":" correctly. The divergence is latent, not live.

IT IS STILL A DIVERGENCE, and it is in the shared derivation. Whoever adds a format whose document can be a bare scalar, or a store that walks the root, will meet it. Two options, both wire lane: change the early return to "" only for an undef path (measure first -- something may depend on the current answer), or record the rule at _path_to_aad so the next reader does not have to re-measure it. The second is cheap and safe.

Not fixed in #36 because it is SOPS.pm's MAC path and the ENV handler does not need it changed.
